  "repository": {
    "excluded": {
      "_comment": "D5/D9: the only construct that suppresses the gate. No inner patterns, so nothing inside is parsed.",
      "begin": "^[ \\t]*((?:(?<!!)!!(?!!)|(?:https?://)?ddot\\.it/)off)[ \\t]*$",
      "end": "^[ \\t]*((?:(?<!!)!!(?!!)|(?:https?://)?ddot\\.it/)on)[ \\t]*$",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "keyword.control.command.ddot"
        }
      },
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "keyword.control.command.ddot"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "comment.block.excluded.ddot"
    },
    "block-verbatim-marked": {
      "_comment": [
        "D7: !!block?end=MARKER. Must precede the blank-line variant.",
        "!! FRAGILE: `end` back-references capture group 8 of `begin` BY NUMBER (\\8).",
        "Adding, removing or reordering ANY capture group in `begin` silently breaks the",
        "terminator -- the block would then run to end of document instead of stopping at the",
        "marker. If you touch `begin`, recount the groups and update `end`, and re-run corpus",
        "case 21-block-end-marker, which is the only thing that catches this.",
        "A named group (?<marker>...) with \\k<marker> does NOT work: vscode-textmate compiles",
        "`begin` and `end` as separate regexes and substitutes the captured TEXT by numeric",
        "index before compiling, so Oniguruma never sees the name and fails with",
        "'undefined name <'. Verified against vscode-oniguruma 2.x. The number is unavoidable."
      ],
      "begin": "^[ \\t]*([^\\r\\n]*?)[ \\t]*(?:((?<!\\.)(?:\\.{4}|\\.{2}[ \\t]+\\.{2})(?!\\.))|((?<!\\.)\\.{2}(?!\\.))[ \\t]*([^\\r\\n]*?)[ \\t]*((?<!\\.)\\.{2}(?!\\.)))[ \\t]*((?:(?<!!)!!(?!!)|(?:https?://)?ddot\\.it/)block)(\\?end=)(\\S+)[ \\t]*$",
      "end": "^[ \\t]*\\8[ \\t]*$",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "entity.name.subject.ddot",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#command"
            }
          ]
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "keyword.operator.doubledot.ddot"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "keyword.operator.doubledot.ddot"
        },
        "4": {
          "name": "entity.name.relation.ddot",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#command"
            }
          ]
        },
        "5": {
          "name": "keyword.operator.doubledot.ddot"
        },
        "6": {
          "name": "keyword.control.command.ddot"
        },
        "7": {
          "name": "variable.parameter.command.ddot"
        },
        "8": {
          "name": "variable.parameter.block-end.ddot"
        }
      },
      "endCaptures": {
        "0": {
          "name": "variable.parameter.block-end.ddot"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "string.unquoted.block.ddot"
    },
    "block-verbatim": {
      "_comment": [
        "D7: plain !!block, terminated by the first blank line.",
        "This rule is correct; it is Shiki that cannot run it. Shiki's per-line loop in",
        "@shikijs/primitive skips empty lines outright (`if (line === \"\") { ...; continue }`)",
        "without calling grammar.tokenizeLine, so grammar state never advances across a blank",
        "line and this rule's terminator never fires. That is an upstream Shiki bug, NOT the",
        "TextMate engine: the blank line never reaches it, which is why `end: ^[ \\t]*$` and",
        "`while: ^[ \\t]*\\S` (non-zero-width) fail identically -- no spelling here avoids it.",
        "Confirmed by patching that guard: corpus case 17-block then passes unmodified.",
        "vscode-textmate (VS Code, the regenerator, conformance-textmate) is unaffected.",
        "17-block is waived in tools/conformance-shiki.mjs, which carries the full analysis.",
        "Case 21 (?end=MARKER) is unaffected -- its terminator is a marker line, not a blank one."
      ],
      "begin": "^[ \\t]*([^\\r\\n]*?)[ \\t]*(?:((?<!\\.)(?:\\.{4}|\\.{2}[ \\t]+\\.{2})(?!\\.))|((?<!\\.)\\.{2}(?!\\.))[ \\t]*([^\\r\\n]*?)[ \\t]*((?<!\\.)\\.{2}(?!\\.)))[ \\t]*((?:(?<!!)!!(?!!)|(?:https?://)?ddot\\.it/)block)[ \\t]*$",
      "end": "^[ \\t]*$",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "entity.name.subject.ddot",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#command"
            }
          ]
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "keyword.operator.doubledot.ddot"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "keyword.operator.doubledot.ddot"
        },
        "4": {
          "name": "entity.name.relation.ddot",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#command"
            }
          ]
        },
        "5": {
          "name": "keyword.operator.doubledot.ddot"
        },
        "6": {
          "name": "keyword.control.command.ddot"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "string.unquoted.block.ddot"
    },
